WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.920
- Welcome to the Huberman Lab Podcast.

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.950
where we discuss science
and science-based tools

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.362
for everyday life.

00:00:06.362 --> 00:00:09.360
[bright music]

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.120
I'm Andrew Huberman, and I'm
a professor of neurobiology

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.180
and ophthalmology at
Stanford School of Medicine.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.160
Today, we are discussing cannabis,

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.500
also referred to as marijuana.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.487
Cannabis includes many different compounds

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:25.020
that have profound impact
on the brain and body,

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.750
so while many of you have
probably heard of THC,

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.140
there are also compounds
in cannabis such as CBD,

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.670
and of course there are different types

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:33.840
or strains of cannabis,

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.450
including sativa strains
and indica strains

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:38.940
and hybrid strains, and believe it or not,

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:41.940
nowadays, there is also
an entire literature,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.010
meaning a scientific
and medicinal literature

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.200
about type one, type two
and type three strains.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.020
I'll explain what all of
that is and how they work.

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:51.270
I'll talk about some of
the medicinal applications

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:52.770
of different strains of cannabis

00:00:52.770 --> 00:00:54.900
and combinations of cannabis strains,

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.600
as well as some of the
potential health hazards

00:00:57.600 --> 00:00:59.280
of cannabis use.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.440
I want to emphasize that any
discussion about cannabis

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.180
has to be framed within the context

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:07.020
that the legality of
cannabis varies tremendously

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.490
depending on where you are in the world,

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.160
so depending on which country you're in

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:12.480
and even which state you're in

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.384
or which area within a country,

00:01:14.384 --> 00:01:17.430
possessing and using and
certainly selling cannabis

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:20.490
can be either highly
illegal or entirely legal

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.280
or decriminalized or largely overlooked.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.440
You, of course, are obligated to know

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:27.247
what those local laws are for you,

00:01:27.247 --> 00:01:30.030
where you live and where you travel.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:32.340
With that said, today's discussion

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:35.100
really will include a full picture

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:38.400
as to where cannabis and the various

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.440
and even very specific
compounds within cannabis

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:44.190
can be extremely useful in
the treatment of some ailments

00:01:44.190 --> 00:01:46.830
and where certain compounds in cannabis

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:50.250
can be extremely dangerous for
certain individuals to use,

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:53.231
in particular, individuals
that have preexisting,

00:01:53.231 --> 00:01:56.220
genetic propensity for psychosis.

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:57.930
That theme is going to
come up again and again,

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.450
but we are also going to talk
about the role of cannabis

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:02.760
in anxiety and depression,

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.470
both positive and negative effects.

00:02:04.470 --> 00:02:05.700
We'll talk about sex differences

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.160
in terms of women versus men

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.960
and how they react
differently to cannabis,

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.550
and I would be entirely remiss

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:14.520
if I didn't include a
conversation about cannabis,

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.850
meaning THC, CBD, hybrid
strains, et cetera

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:20.490
in creativity and different
modes of thinking,

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.620
because as many of you probably know

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.570
or at least have heard about,

00:02:24.570 --> 00:02:27.270
cannabis can impact the way that we think,

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:29.490
the types of memory systems we can access

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:31.380
and what's called convergent
and divergent thinking,

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:33.720
which is one way of conceptualizing

00:02:33.720 --> 00:02:36.870
what is commonly referred
to as creativity.

00:02:36.870 --> 00:02:39.270
So today's discussion is going to include

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.470
a lot of information,

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.960
but I promise to make it clear
and accessible to all of you,

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.790
regardless of whether or
not you have a background

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.350
in biology or not,

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:49.380
and today's discussion
will also be quite nuanced.

00:02:49.380 --> 00:02:51.180
You'll find me routinely reading

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.340
directly from specific research papers,

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:56.252
something that of course we
always do on this podcast,

00:02:56.252 --> 00:02:57.960
but today I'm really going to dig

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:01.440
into some of the finer points
of the methodology in papers

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.810
and some of the statistics that were used

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:06.660
and the specific populations
of people that were studied,

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:07.920
because as it turns out,

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.750
there are instances that we will discuss

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:13.170
in which the use of cannabis
can be immensely beneficial

00:03:13.170 --> 00:03:16.590
to one group and yet can
be entirely detrimental

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:19.097
to another group, even
at equivalent dosages

00:03:19.097 --> 00:03:21.600
and depending on a number
of different factors,

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.820
so we will discuss what those factors are.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.560
Just to give you a brief overview

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:28.560
of the kind of structure I'm
going to put on today's episode,

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.470
we will review of course,
cannabis and its various forms.

00:03:31.470 --> 00:03:32.550
I'll talk about some of the biology,

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:36.150
but we are going to really
drill into how dosage,

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:39.461
that is the concentration
of THC relative to CBD,

00:03:39.461 --> 00:03:41.700
impacts whether or not cannabis

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.140
is going to have one effect or another.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:46.320
We will also talk about
the frequency of use,

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:49.080
daily use, multiple times per day use,

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.510
weekly use or monthly or occasional use.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:53.640
We will also talk about
different professions

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.860
and how some people may have
a little bit more leeway

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:58.620
in terms of whether or not
they decide to use cannabis

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:02.310
or any of its various component
chemical constituents,

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.920
that is CBD or THC, et cetera.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.720
And for other professions,

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:08.310
it might be entirely inappropriate

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:10.650
because of the particular
kinds of cognitive tasks

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:12.120
those professions demand.

00:04:12.120 --> 00:04:14.760
We will also talk about
genetic predisposition,

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.540
again, sex differences, hormone effects,

00:04:16.540 --> 00:04:18.330
and I will also touch on what I think

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:20.250
is the most important variable

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:22.620
in determining whether or not cannabis

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:27.000
is right or wrong for
you, and that is your age

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:28.740
at which you are considering starting

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:31.230
or continuing use or ceasing use.

00:04:31.230 --> 00:04:34.110
What I can assure you is that
by the end of today's podcast,

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:37.410
you will have a quite thorough
understanding of cannabis,

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:39.090
how it works, what it does,

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.950
what its potential benefits can be,

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:43.050
what its potential hazards are,

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.850
and whether or not it's right for you

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.020
and the people that you know.

