00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:12.420
Let's talk about cannabis,
and when we refer to cannabis,

00:15:12.420 --> 00:15:15.780
we are indeed referring to
marijuana or the marijuana plant.

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:19.070
Now, cannabis plants
come in different strains

00:15:19.070 --> 00:15:22.320
or different varieties,
and those different strains

00:15:22.320 --> 00:15:24.893
are indeed different genetic strains.

00:15:24.893 --> 00:15:26.970
So just as animals and humans

00:15:26.970 --> 00:15:28.560
have different genetic backgrounds,

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:30.180
and they can be crossed to one another

00:15:30.180 --> 00:15:34.830
to yield further genetic
variation in the offspring,

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:37.171
plants can be hybridized to one another

00:15:37.171 --> 00:15:39.600
in various ways through grafting

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:42.240
or through the use of different
types of seed combinations,

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:45.270
et cetera, in order to
generate different strains.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:47.850
There are also naturally
occurring differences

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:49.560
in the strains of plants,

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:52.530
and the cannabis plant is no exception.

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.570
So for instance, in the context

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:56.250
of the discussion about cannabis

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:59.195
and its medicinal uses
and recreational uses,

00:15:59.195 --> 00:16:03.512
we need to distinguish
between the sativa variety,

00:16:03.512 --> 00:16:08.430
the indica variety, a
variety called ruderalis

00:16:08.430 --> 00:16:10.140
that's not often discussed,

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:14.010
and hybrids of sativa,
indica and ruderalis.

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:16.050
Before diving into the
different strains of cannabis

00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:17.520
and how they impact the brain embody,

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:20.610
both similarly and differently,

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:22.920
I want to emphasize
that the cannabis plant

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:26.250
contains a number of different
psychoactive compounds.

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:30.060
Now, the most powerful of
those compounds is THC.

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:34.779
The technical name for it is
delta-9-tetrahydrocannabinol.

00:16:34.779 --> 00:16:37.980
But THC, as I'll refer to it,

00:16:37.980 --> 00:16:40.230
is just one of the psychoactive

00:16:40.230 --> 00:16:43.263
and biologically active
compounds within cannabis plants.

00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:48.780
There's also CBD, which
is technically referred to

00:16:48.780 --> 00:16:52.923
as cannabidiol, and cannabidiol, CBD,

00:16:52.923 --> 00:16:56.670
is known to be used for
things like pain management,

00:16:56.670 --> 00:16:59.610
anxiety management and
other medicinal purposes.

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:03.090
We will talk about the efficacy
of CBD for those purposes,

00:17:03.090 --> 00:17:04.860
as well as some of, believe it or not,

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:06.233
some of the dangers of CBD,

00:17:06.233 --> 00:17:09.183
depending on where it's sourced
and the dosage, et cetera.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:15.380
So we've got THC, CBD and
also CBN or cannabinol.

00:17:16.013 --> 00:17:18.390
CBN is less often discussed.

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:19.650
You're going to hear a lot less

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:22.488
about CBN containing products out there,

00:17:22.488 --> 00:17:24.150
CBN containing medicines,

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:25.480
but it is relevant to today's discussion,

00:17:25.480 --> 00:17:27.090
so it will come up a bit.

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:29.400
Now, I will be sure to
provide more specificity

00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:33.125
to what I'm about to say,
but very broadly speaking,

00:17:33.125 --> 00:17:35.670
THC is largely responsible

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:38.733
for the psychoactive effects of cannabis,

00:17:38.733 --> 00:17:42.090
that is the changes in mood,
the changes in bodily state

00:17:42.090 --> 00:17:44.700
and sensation, et cetera.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:47.280
Whereas CBD and to some extent,

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:52.200
CBN, have profound effects
on the brain and body,

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:54.420
but they don't tend to
give people the sensation

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:58.110
of altered perception,
altered mood, et cetera.

00:17:58.110 --> 00:18:00.685
Some people might say they are
not the component of cannabis

00:18:00.685 --> 00:18:03.150
that, quote unquote, gets you high,

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:04.680
although today, we will really drill into

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.720
what the high itself represents

00:18:06.720 --> 00:18:09.390
in terms of chemical
systems in the brain body.

00:18:09.390 --> 00:18:12.026
And what we will soon learn is that

00:18:12.026 --> 00:18:15.810
what we think of as being
high actually includes

00:18:15.810 --> 00:18:17.880
a number of different changes
in the brain and body,

00:18:17.880 --> 00:18:21.030
some of which can be
best explained by CBD,

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:23.400
not by THC, which runs counter

00:18:23.400 --> 00:18:26.430
to what most people out
there know and believe.

00:18:26.430 --> 00:18:30.900
So broadly speaking, we
have THC, CBD and CBN.

00:18:30.900 --> 00:18:33.180
But I want to point out
that the cannabis plant

00:18:33.180 --> 00:18:35.122
has over 70, seven-zero,

00:18:35.122 --> 00:18:37.290
70 different psychoactive compounds,

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:40.140
many of which still have not been studied

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:42.180
in isolation and in detail.

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:44.799
So there's a big future
of research for cannabis

00:18:44.799 --> 00:18:48.360
and for THC and THC-related
psychoactive compounds,

00:18:48.360 --> 00:18:50.790
as well as for CBD and CBN.

00:18:50.790 --> 00:18:52.189
Today we're mainly going to focus

00:18:52.189 --> 00:18:55.650
on THC and CBD, as I mentioned before.

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:57.360
I should also point out
that the cannabis plant

00:18:57.360 --> 00:19:00.797
has over 400 biologically
active compounds.

00:19:00.797 --> 00:19:02.715
So these are biologically active compounds

00:19:02.715 --> 00:19:06.690
that may or may not have
psychoactive properties,

00:19:06.690 --> 00:19:09.480
that may or may not be useful
for pain relief, et cetera.

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:12.810
Again, there is a vast
landscape for exploration

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:16.285
of the cannabis plant and of
hemp for what they include

00:19:16.285 --> 00:19:20.040
that could be beneficial
to us or detrimental to us,

00:19:20.040 --> 00:19:21.840
so again, a lot more work to do.

00:19:21.840 --> 00:19:23.910
Today, we're going to really
try and stay on target

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:25.770
with what we already know

00:19:25.770 --> 00:19:27.974
and where there are
certain exciting mysteries

00:19:27.974 --> 00:19:29.490
or intriguing mysteries

00:19:29.490 --> 00:19:31.530
about what we ought to explore more.

00:19:31.530 --> 00:19:33.180
I will certainly highlight those.

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:36.090
Let's go back to the different strains

00:19:36.090 --> 00:19:38.831
of the cannabis plant,
sativa, indica and ruderalis

00:19:38.831 --> 00:19:41.670
and explore how each of those

00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:44.520
differentially impacts the brain and body,

00:19:44.520 --> 00:19:46.590
because therein I think
we can start to learn

00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:48.600
a lot about this incredible plant

00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:50.310
that is the cannabis plant.

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:53.160
And whether or not you
are a user of cannabis

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:56.490
or whether or not you are
entirely opposed to cannabis use,

00:19:56.490 --> 00:19:58.500
understanding how cannabis works

00:19:58.500 --> 00:20:01.620
in the brain and body, itself,
is absolutely fascinating

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:04.830
and can teach you a lot about
how your brain and body work

00:20:04.830 --> 00:20:07.890
at a basic level and
can tell you a lot about

00:20:07.890 --> 00:20:10.290
how your brain and body will
react to different life events

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:13.260
and how your mood is
established and stabilized,

00:20:13.260 --> 00:20:15.896
and how your appetite is
established and stabilized

00:20:15.896 --> 00:20:17.190
and so on.

00:20:17.190 --> 00:20:19.140
So we have the three
major strains of cannabis,

00:20:19.140 --> 00:20:21.930
sativa, indica and ruderalis.

00:20:21.930 --> 00:20:23.700
And for sake of today's conversation,

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:26.040
we can pretty much cross off ruderalis.

00:20:26.040 --> 00:20:28.260
It's not often consumed,

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:32.310
and components of ruderalis
are not often consumed

00:20:32.310 --> 00:20:34.383
for medicinal or recreational purposes.

00:20:35.520 --> 00:20:37.593
Let's focus on sativa and indica.

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:42.960
People will consume the
sativa variety of cannabis

00:20:42.960 --> 00:20:47.310
either by edible or by smoking cannabis,

00:20:47.310 --> 00:20:50.040
or they will consume the
indica variety of cannabis,

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:53.400
again by edible or by smoking cannabis,

00:20:53.400 --> 00:20:56.370
or sometimes they will take
it in a transdermal form

00:20:56.370 --> 00:20:58.380
or a sublingual form.

00:20:58.380 --> 00:20:59.520
There are a bunch of different ways

00:20:59.520 --> 00:21:02.520
to get the cannabis into the body,

00:21:02.520 --> 00:21:06.330
but there's a clear distinction
between sativa and indica

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:09.509
that actually shows up first
in the structure of the plant.

00:21:09.509 --> 00:21:14.160
At their extremes, meaning
in a pure strain of sativa,

00:21:14.160 --> 00:21:16.710
it tends to be a taller
plant, a longer stock,

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:17.670
believe it or not,

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:20.820
and actually the length of the
leaves is quite a bit longer,

00:21:20.820 --> 00:21:24.558
whereas the indica plant tends
to be more short and stout.

00:21:24.558 --> 00:21:27.900
And, for those aficionados out there,

00:21:27.900 --> 00:21:29.880
I'm sure you know a lot of
the other specific features

00:21:29.880 --> 00:21:31.320
of sativa versus indica,

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:34.380
but already what we're talking
about is the same plant,

00:21:34.380 --> 00:21:38.310
cannabis, with two very
different morphologies or shapes.

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:40.087
You might say, "Well, why is
this interesting or important

00:21:40.087 --> 00:21:42.652
"to how it affects me
or affects other people

00:21:42.652 --> 00:21:44.850
"for medicinal or recreational purposes?"

00:21:44.850 --> 00:21:47.730
Well, it turns out that even
though they are the same plant,

00:21:47.730 --> 00:21:49.339
these two different genetic varieties,

00:21:49.339 --> 00:21:52.740
because of the way that they grow

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:54.330
and the way they capture sunlight

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:57.191
and the way, believe it or
not, that the different plants

00:21:57.191 --> 00:21:59.820
within that strain
interact with one another,

00:21:59.820 --> 00:22:00.960
'cause believe it or not,

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:02.970
plants are interacting with one another,

00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:04.920
they actually bring different elements

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:07.320
of the psychoactive compounds
to different components

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:09.370
within the leaves and the so-called buds.

00:22:10.590 --> 00:22:12.630
The takeaway is that when consumed,

00:22:12.630 --> 00:22:14.520
and when I say consumed,
I want to be very clear,

00:22:14.520 --> 00:22:17.910
I don't necessarily just
mean oral consumption

00:22:17.910 --> 00:22:22.080
or eating cannabis sativa by edible,

00:22:22.080 --> 00:22:25.080
I also mean smoking it,
and that could be...

00:22:25.080 --> 00:22:27.780
people will, just like with tobacco,

00:22:27.780 --> 00:22:30.270
the way that they bring
the psychoactive components

00:22:30.270 --> 00:22:32.730
into their bloodstream and
into their brain and body

00:22:32.730 --> 00:22:36.300
is to essentially heat the dried leaves

00:22:36.300 --> 00:22:38.640
of the cannabis plant.

00:22:38.640 --> 00:22:42.750
Then the heat liberates some
of the psychoactive components

00:22:42.750 --> 00:22:44.610
that when inhaled into the lungs,

00:22:44.610 --> 00:22:46.890
because the lungs include
a lot of vasculature,

00:22:46.890 --> 00:22:50.430
a lot of basically blood
vessels and capillaries,

00:22:50.430 --> 00:22:53.730
that the psychoactive components

00:22:53.730 --> 00:22:54.990
are actually directly absorbed

00:22:54.990 --> 00:22:56.490
from the lungs into the bloodstream,

00:22:56.490 --> 00:22:58.080
and they can cross into the bloodstream

00:22:58.080 --> 00:23:00.300
and permeate throughout the body

00:23:00.300 --> 00:23:02.280
and cross the so-called
blood brain barrier.

00:23:02.280 --> 00:23:06.840
So in other words, burning
the plant liberates the smoke

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:09.690
that contains the psychoactive compounds,

00:23:09.690 --> 00:23:11.550
and those are inhaled into the lungs

00:23:11.550 --> 00:23:13.170
and then get into the brain and body

00:23:13.170 --> 00:23:14.610
and act on the brain and body.

00:23:14.610 --> 00:23:17.250
And the major effect of sativa varieties

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:19.980
are to create a high, if you will,

00:23:19.980 --> 00:23:21.030
and I'm putting this in air quotes

00:23:21.030 --> 00:23:22.470
for those of you that are listening,

00:23:22.470 --> 00:23:24.480
but to also act as a stimulant.

00:23:24.480 --> 00:23:26.310
The sativa varieties tend to make people

00:23:26.310 --> 00:23:29.070
feel invigorated, somewhat alert.

00:23:29.070 --> 00:23:31.080
It doesn't tend to be
as much of a sedative

00:23:31.080 --> 00:23:32.760
as some of the other varieties.

00:23:32.760 --> 00:23:35.190
Some people report
heightened sense of focus

00:23:35.190 --> 00:23:36.720
or heightened sense of creativity.

00:23:36.720 --> 00:23:37.920
We'll talk a little bit later on

00:23:37.920 --> 00:23:39.270
as to whether or not they actually

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:41.790
are achieving heightened
levels of focus and creativity,

00:23:41.790 --> 00:23:43.500
or whether or not they
just perceive themselves

00:23:43.500 --> 00:23:45.327
to have heightened levels
of focus and creativity.

00:23:45.327 --> 00:23:47.910
The sativa varieties tend to make people

00:23:47.910 --> 00:23:50.550
feel a little bit less susceptible

00:23:50.550 --> 00:23:52.800
to pain and noxious stimuli,

00:23:52.800 --> 00:23:55.950
which are basically stimuli
that you don't like.

00:23:55.950 --> 00:24:00.950
So the sativa varieties are
often prescribed or are used

00:24:01.120 --> 00:24:05.220
in the recreational context
for pain management and relief.

00:24:05.220 --> 00:24:07.620
Basically, the sativa variety is known

00:24:07.620 --> 00:24:10.500
to include a head biased effect.

00:24:10.500 --> 00:24:12.960
So here, we're talking
about subjective effects,

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:14.220
and of course these will vary

00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:16.020
from one individual to the next.

00:24:16.020 --> 00:24:18.080
Some people will smoke cannabis sativa

00:24:18.080 --> 00:24:20.320
or ingest cannabis sativa orally

00:24:21.180 --> 00:24:24.450
and will feel an entirely
different array of effects,

00:24:24.450 --> 00:24:26.460
but most people, the majority of people

00:24:26.460 --> 00:24:30.288
experience a head-centered
high, alertness, focus

00:24:30.288 --> 00:24:33.060
and a sense that they're more creative.

00:24:33.060 --> 00:24:36.330
Contrast that with the
indica varieties of cannabis,

00:24:36.330 --> 00:24:40.980
and when people smoke or eat
or ingest indica varieties,

00:24:40.980 --> 00:24:43.140
the psychoactive components of indica,

00:24:43.140 --> 00:24:44.670
and again, this is pure indica,

00:24:44.670 --> 00:24:47.850
so not hybridized with sativa
at all, but just pure indica,

00:24:47.850 --> 00:24:51.090
tend to lead to more full-bodied effects.

00:24:51.090 --> 00:24:55.380
People report feeling more
complete, full-body relaxation,

00:24:55.380 --> 00:24:57.600
more of a sedative effect.

00:24:57.600 --> 00:25:00.480
Indica cannabis is often prescribed

00:25:00.480 --> 00:25:02.160
and/or used recreationally

00:25:02.160 --> 00:25:04.890
in order to achieve a state of sleep

00:25:04.890 --> 00:25:09.300
or to help relieve anxiety,
so less of a stimulant effect.

00:25:09.300 --> 00:25:11.040
And we will talk about why,

00:25:11.040 --> 00:25:12.538
literally, the underlying neural circuits

00:25:12.538 --> 00:25:16.350
that lead to the sativa
variety causing more

00:25:16.350 --> 00:25:19.800
of a elevated mood and a
head high, if you will,

00:25:19.800 --> 00:25:23.040
and the indica variety as being
more full body relaxation.

00:25:23.040 --> 00:25:24.450
One of the ways to
remember the distinction

00:25:24.450 --> 00:25:27.600
between the effects of cannabis
sativa and cannabis indica

00:25:27.600 --> 00:25:30.630
was relayed to me by a friend
who actually was a chronic,

00:25:30.630 --> 00:25:34.830
meaning every day, all
day, consumer of marijuana.

00:25:34.830 --> 00:25:36.720
He basically smoked marijuana for 20 years

00:25:36.720 --> 00:25:39.030
before quitting about
four or five years ago,

00:25:39.030 --> 00:25:42.270
and he said that indica
is often referred to

00:25:42.270 --> 00:25:45.900
as 'in-da-couch,' meaning
laid back in the couch.

00:25:45.900 --> 00:25:47.610
And that can help you remember

00:25:47.610 --> 00:25:49.423
that the indica varieties of cannabis

00:25:49.423 --> 00:25:52.847
do tend to be more
sedative in their effects.

00:25:52.847 --> 00:25:54.570
Okay, so there's sativa
and there's indica,

00:25:54.570 --> 00:25:56.790
and then now there are hybrid strains.

00:25:56.790 --> 00:26:00.240
So marijuana growers and
people who specialize

00:26:00.240 --> 00:26:03.469
in creating novel varieties
of the cannabis plant,

00:26:03.469 --> 00:26:05.820
again, I'm using the words
cannabis and marijuana

00:26:05.820 --> 00:26:08.040
more or less interchangeably here,

00:26:08.040 --> 00:26:12.240
they are very good at
creating new strains of plant

00:26:12.240 --> 00:26:17.240
that might be 25% sativa and
75% indica or vice versa,

00:26:17.340 --> 00:26:19.548
or 50/50 or 90/10.

00:26:19.548 --> 00:26:21.660
Essentially, what's happening nowadays

00:26:21.660 --> 00:26:26.370
is that through plant biology,
plant genetics, I should say,

00:26:26.370 --> 00:26:29.010
growers are getting quite efficient

00:26:29.010 --> 00:26:31.590
at creating a variety of different strains

00:26:31.590 --> 00:26:35.880
of the marijuana plant that
give rise to very nuanced

00:26:35.880 --> 00:26:39.090
and distinct effects on brain and body.

00:26:39.090 --> 00:26:42.690
In fact, so much so, that
there's now a new nomenclature,

00:26:42.690 --> 00:26:46.560
a new language emerging around cannabis

00:26:46.560 --> 00:26:48.810
and the development of
novel strains of cannabis

00:26:48.810 --> 00:26:51.810
for medicinal and/or
recreational purposes.

00:26:51.810 --> 00:26:54.534
And while this might
sound a little bit medical

00:26:54.534 --> 00:26:58.020
or a little bit clinical to
some people, believe it or not,

00:26:58.020 --> 00:27:00.540
this is the nomenclature
that is now typically used.

00:27:00.540 --> 00:27:04.292
People still refer to the sativa,
indica and hybrid strains,

00:27:04.292 --> 00:27:06.540
but there's now also a description

00:27:06.540 --> 00:27:11.280
of so-called type one, type
two and type three strains

00:27:11.280 --> 00:27:14.850
for any given sativa,
indica or hybrid strain.

00:27:14.850 --> 00:27:17.250
Okay, so just to put this
clearly in your mind,

00:27:17.250 --> 00:27:20.490
you've got sativa varieties,
that is pure sativa varieties.

00:27:20.490 --> 00:27:24.450
You have indica varieties,
again, pure indica,

00:27:24.450 --> 00:27:26.820
and then you have hybrid varieties,

00:27:26.820 --> 00:27:28.710
and beneath each of those,

00:27:28.710 --> 00:27:32.699
you have type one, type
two and type three strains

00:27:32.699 --> 00:27:37.699
of indica, sativa or hybrid varieties.

00:27:38.190 --> 00:27:41.370
What are type one, type
two and type three?

00:27:41.370 --> 00:27:45.009
Well, type one, type two
and type three strains

00:27:45.009 --> 00:27:47.790
are strains that have varying amounts

00:27:47.790 --> 00:27:51.363
or ratios of THC to CBD.

00:27:52.200 --> 00:27:54.840
So for instance, type one strain,

00:27:54.840 --> 00:27:58.170
so for instance, you could
have a pure sativa, type one,

00:27:58.170 --> 00:28:01.829
or a type one pure sativa
or a type one indica.

00:28:01.829 --> 00:28:04.260
Those are going to have
the greatest amount

00:28:04.260 --> 00:28:06.570
of THC relative to CBD.

00:28:06.570 --> 00:28:08.280
And I really want to emphasize this,

00:28:08.280 --> 00:28:11.058
understanding the ratio of THC to CBD

00:28:11.058 --> 00:28:14.430
can help explain a lot
or even predict a lot

00:28:14.430 --> 00:28:18.810
about how a given strain of
cannabis will impact somebody.

00:28:18.810 --> 00:28:22.558
For instance, because THC
is largely responsible

00:28:22.558 --> 00:28:27.558
for the typical psychoactive
components of cannabis,

00:28:27.613 --> 00:28:31.380
so what I mean here is, if
somebody's ingesting sativa,

00:28:31.380 --> 00:28:34.650
and it routinely makes
them feel more energized,

00:28:34.650 --> 00:28:36.480
elevates their mood,

00:28:36.480 --> 00:28:38.310
it gives them a heightened
sense of creativity,

00:28:38.310 --> 00:28:40.350
if that's what they experience,

00:28:40.350 --> 00:28:42.720
and they're taking a
type one version of that,

00:28:42.720 --> 00:28:47.241
that means that it's quite rich
in THC and very little CBD.

00:28:47.241 --> 00:28:51.300
However, if they were to take
a type one version of sativa,

00:28:51.300 --> 00:28:53.610
and it feels far too strong,
like too much energy,

00:28:53.610 --> 00:28:55.530
or they felt like they were
too much in their head,

00:28:55.530 --> 00:28:58.793
nowadays, there are strains of sativa

00:28:58.793 --> 00:29:01.590
that have been genetically engineered,

00:29:01.590 --> 00:29:03.750
and I don't mean by an
engineer tinkering away

00:29:03.750 --> 00:29:08.640
with gene engineering in
a CRISPR creating mutes,

00:29:08.640 --> 00:29:10.050
but literally by hybridizing,

00:29:10.050 --> 00:29:12.860
crossing different plants to one another,

00:29:12.860 --> 00:29:15.150
creating in a natural context,

00:29:15.150 --> 00:29:16.983
the same way plants in the outside world

00:29:16.983 --> 00:29:19.653
would sometimes hybridize to one another,

00:29:20.790 --> 00:29:23.610
creating a variety
that's perhaps type two,

00:29:23.610 --> 00:29:28.503
which is going to have
less THC and more CBD,

00:29:28.503 --> 00:29:31.560
or a type three, which is
going to be very high CBD

00:29:31.560 --> 00:29:33.450
and very little THC,

00:29:33.450 --> 00:29:36.069
and the same is also true
for the indica varieties.

00:29:36.069 --> 00:29:38.220
So I want to make sure that
everyone understands this,

00:29:38.220 --> 00:29:39.270
because it becomes very important

00:29:39.270 --> 00:29:41.550
for understanding the biology of cannabis

00:29:41.550 --> 00:29:46.425
and predicting positive versus
negative effects of cannabis.

00:29:46.425 --> 00:29:49.470
Sativa has this stimulant-like effect

00:29:49.470 --> 00:29:51.630
and tends to be more of
a head high, if you will.

00:29:51.630 --> 00:29:53.280
Indica tends to be more full-body,

00:29:53.280 --> 00:29:56.073
then lead to more in-da-couch,
as I refer to it before,

00:29:56.923 --> 00:30:01.622
pun intended, deep relaxation,
reduce insomnia, et cetera.

00:30:01.622 --> 00:30:03.750
Now, within each of
those sativa and indica,

00:30:03.750 --> 00:30:05.220
you have type one, type
two and type three,

00:30:05.220 --> 00:30:09.240
and that has everything
to do with how much THC,

00:30:09.240 --> 00:30:12.180
which is the dominant
psychoactive compound,

00:30:12.180 --> 00:30:15.990
versus CBD, which has other
effects, mainly on the body,

00:30:15.990 --> 00:30:18.360
but not so much on the brain

00:30:18.360 --> 00:30:20.100
and modes of thinking and mood, et cetera,

00:30:20.100 --> 00:30:22.230
how much THC versus CBD is present.

00:30:22.230 --> 00:30:25.140
And again, type one is THC dominant,

00:30:25.140 --> 00:30:28.290
type two, equal ratios, if
you will, of THC and CBD,

00:30:28.290 --> 00:30:30.858
and type three tend to be high CBD.

00:30:30.858 --> 00:30:32.760
Okay, so already we've got
some categorization here

00:30:32.760 --> 00:30:34.680
that hopefully isn't overwhelming to you,

00:30:34.680 --> 00:30:37.140
but this turns out to
be extremely important

00:30:37.140 --> 00:30:39.166
if you want to understand
how cannabis works

00:30:39.166 --> 00:30:41.400
and predict the effects of cannabis.

